{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: give the test suite a timeout budget the loaded machine can meet.\n\nWhy. go test's default per-package timeout is 10 minutes. cmd/gs took between 325 and 854 seconds across 33 full runs on this machine on 2026-09-16 and 17 while other lanes were running, and internal/app between 177 and 238 seconds. Three runs exceeded ten minutes and reported \"panic: test timed out\", which once let a lane publish a green claim over a killed gate. Hosted CI runs the same suite under -race in about six minutes, so the package is not broken; it is slow, and the Makefile's test and race targets carry no -timeout. Every actor now has to remember to pass -timeout 40m by hand.\n\nOutcome. make test and make race pass a timeout the package needs, the contributor page states the figure and why, and the ten slowest tests in cmd/gs are listed in the artifact text with, for each, whether it repeats a fixture another test already builds. Reducing the runtime is a separate request if that list justifies one.","body":{"branch":"request/test-timeout-budget","conditions":"1. Makefile test and race targets pass an explicit -timeout large enough for the observed range with margin, and any documented full-suite command in docs or SKILL.md uses the same. 2. The artifact text lists the ten slowest cmd/gs tests by wall time from one run, with the fixture each builds. 3. No test is skipped, shortened or made conditional to meet the budget. 4. go test ./... green at the exact head; independent review by codex; ratified; landed on main and pushed.","target_head":"3c7f13c79cb079ef0f40961d51d7ff4f350787c5","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}